          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
          %ul
            %li
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+categories"} regular categories
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lex+categories"} lex categories
            %li
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+categories"} exact categories
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lex+categories"} lex categories
            %li
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+categories"} exact categories
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+categories"} regular categories
          %p
            have
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+adjunction"} (2-)monadic
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
          %p
            In the third case the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion"} completion
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+monad"} lax-idempotent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+completion"} free completion
            %em regular completion
            and
            %em exact completion
            are also commonly used for the first two cases. To disambiguate the second and third cases the phrases
            %em ex/lex completion
            and
            %em ex/reg completion
            are also used, and so by analogy the first case is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em reg/lex completion
          %p
            In fact, the reg/lex and ex/lex completion can be applied to a category that merely has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+finite+limits"} weak finite limits
            %em all
            of these types of these completions is the 2-category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unary+sites"} unary sites
          %h2#constructions Constructions
          %h3#TheExLexCompletion The ex/lex completion
          %p
            There are several constructions of the ex/lex completion. Perhaps the quickest one to state (Hu-Tholen 1996) is that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
            is the full subcategory of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
            spanned by those presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              admits a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↠
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(X)\twoheadrightarrow F
              from a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaf"} representable presheaf
            %li
              with the additional property that if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\rightrightarrows y(X)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↠
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(X)\twoheadrightarrow F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              also admits a regular epi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(Z)\to K
              from a representable presheaf.
          %p
            A more explicit construction is as follows. Let us think, informally, of the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presets"} presets
            and the morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as “proofs”. An object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex} = C_{ex/lex}
            will then be a “set” or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/setoid"} setoid
            constructed from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-equivalence+relations"} pseudo-equivalence relations
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %ul
            %li
              an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
              and
            %li
              a parallel pair
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t\colon R\rightrightarrows X
            %li
              there exists an arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\colon X\to R
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s i = t i = 1_X
            %li
              there exists an arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v\colon R\to R
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s v = t
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mi v
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t v = s
            %li
              there exists an arrow
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\colon R\times_X R \to R
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s c = s \pi_1
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t c = t \pi_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has merely weak finite limits, we assert this for some, and hence every, weak pullback
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %msubsup
                        %mo ×
                        %mi X
                        %mi w
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\times^w_X R
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t)\colon R\to X\times X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            or internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1,x_2)
            as giving a collection of “reasons” or “proofs” that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 \mathrel{R} x_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            supplies a uniform proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mathrel{R} x
            for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            supplies a uniform proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mathrel{R} y
            implies
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \mathrel{R} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            supplies a uniform proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mathrel{R} y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \mathrel{R} z
            imply
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mathrel{R} z
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\rightrightarrows X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\rightrightarrows Y
            are two pseudo-equivalence relations, a morphism between them in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            is defined to be a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1\colon R\to S
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s f_1 = f s
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t f_1 = f t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1
            supplies a uniform proof that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} R
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mathrel{R} y
            then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} S
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \mathrel{S} f(y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\colon X\to Y
            to be
            %em equal
            if there exists a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon X\to S
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mi h
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s h = f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mi h
                  %mo =
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t h = g
            (that is, a uniform proof that
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "thickmathspace", :rspace => "thickmathspace"} S
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \mathrel{S} g(x)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⇉
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S\rightrightarrows Y
            is a pseudo-equivalence relation, this defines an actual equivalence relation on the morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi ex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
          %p
            We have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_{ex}
            sending an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the pseudo-equivalence relation
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⇉
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\rightrightarrows X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            is exact, that this embedding preserves finite limits, and that it is universal with respect to lex functors from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            into exact categories.
          %p There are also other constructions. Of course, the ex/lex completion can also be obtained by composing (any construction of) the reg/lex completion with (any construction of) the ex/reg completion.
          %h3#the_reglex_completion The reg/lex completion
          %p
            The reg/lex completion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi reg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi lex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}= C_{reg/lex}
            of a lex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is perhaps most succinctly described as the subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            consisting of those objects which admit monomorphisms into objects of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em all
            quotients of pseudo-equivalence relations in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
            of morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi ex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
          %p
            For instance, if we regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            as a full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
            as above, then we can likewise regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
            as the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
            determined by those presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              admits a regular epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↠
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(X) \twoheadrightarrow F
              from a representable presheaf, and
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              admits a monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\rightarrowtail y(Z)
              into a representable presheaf.
          %p
            If we construct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            using pseudo-equivalence relations, as above, then we can characterize the pseudo-equivalence relations which we need to form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
            as precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pairs"} kernel pairs
            of morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (or finite families of such). Therefore, we obtain an equivalent definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
            as follows. Its objects are morphisms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (regarded as stand-ins for their formally added images). A morphism from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon X\to Y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\colon Z\to W
            should be a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Z
            for which there exists an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1
            relating the kernel of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            to the kernel of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the kernel of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon X\to Y
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\colon Z\to W
            to be certain morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f}\colon X\to W
            which factor through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            (non-uniquely). We still have to impose the condition that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            should preserve the kernel pairs, but in terms of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f}
            this is simply the statement that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f} r = \overline{f} s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r,s)
            is the kernel pair of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
            given in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          %p
            We can then verify that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
            is regular, that we have a full and faithful functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi reg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_{reg}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to regular categories. Again, there are also other constructions.
          %p
            Also, just as for the free exact completion, the construction works essentially the same if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has only weak finite limits. In this case, instead of the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi ex
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
            admitting a monomorphism to a single object of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#the_exreg_completion The ex/reg completion
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is regular, a quick definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
            is as the full subcategory of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+coverage"} regular coverage
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            spanned by those sheaves which are quotients of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            A more explicit description can be obtained by first passing from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/allegory"} allegory
            of internal relations, then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+idempotent"} splitting
            the idempotents which are equivalence relations in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
            are congruences in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+relation"} entire
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+relation"} functional
            relative to the given congruences.
          %h3#the_higher_categorical_approach The higher categorical approach
          %p
            A somewhat more unified approach to all these completions can be obtained as follows. Observe that in the classical situation (that is, in the presence of choice),
            %em sets
            can be identified with all of the following:
          %ul
            %li
              0-trivial
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relations"} equivalence relations
            %li
              0-trivial
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoids"} 2-groupoids
            %li and so on…
            %li
              0-trivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-groupoids"} n-groupoids
              for any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\le n \le \infty
          %p
            In the absence of choice, this is still true as long as the morphisms between 0-trivial n-groupoids are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %mi reg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{reg/lex}
              can be identified with the category whose objects are 0-trivial groupoids, and whose morphisms are natural isomorphism classes of functors.
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set_{ex/lex}
              can be identified with the category whose objects are 0-trivial 2-groupoids, and whose morphisms are pseudonatural equivalence classes of 2-functors. In the notion of 2-groupoid here we also demand that each 1-cell be equipped with a
              %em specified
              inverse
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
          %p
            This idea can be generalized to provide alternate constructions of the completions for an arbitrary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with finite limits. The notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            make perfect sense for any
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-groupoid," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em structure
            of “inverse-assigning” morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=(n-1)
            = succeed "-cells" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mi triv
                  %mi n
                  %mi Gpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 triv n Gpd(C)
            for the category of such things and internal
            = succeed "-natural" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                It is fairly clear from the above explicit description that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is the full subcategory of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mi triv
                      %mn 1
                      %mi Gpd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 triv 1 Gpd(C)
                determined by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pairs"} kernel pairs
                (which are
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is already exact, so that every congruence is a kernel pair, then
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi reg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                        %mo ≃
                        %mn 0
                        %mi triv
                        %mn 1
                        %mi Gpd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}\simeq 0 triv 1 Gpd(C)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is always equivalent to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mi triv
                        %mn 2
                        %mi Gpd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 triv 2 Gpd(C)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                with specified inverse equivalences for every 1-cell. There is then a unique way to add 2-cells to make it a 0-trivial bigroupoid.
          %p
            It is not clear how 0-trivial
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\gt 2
            %em iterated
            reg/lex and ex/lex completions can be identified with some type of internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+category"} n-fold category
          %p
            Now if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is already regular, then we can define a notion of internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            between internal
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi ex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi reg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
              is equivalent to the category of 0-trivial 1-groupoids, and natural isomorphism classes of internal anafunctors between them.
          %p
            Again, it is not entirely clear how the 0-trivial
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\gt 1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"} me
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi ex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi reg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\ge 1
          %h3#completions_of_unary_sites Completions of unary sites
          %p
            The descriptions of the ex/lex and ex/reg completions in terms of pseudo-equivalence relations and equivalence relations, respectively, have a common generalization. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unary+site"} unary site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ←
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Z\leftarrow Y
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %em local unary pre-pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ P &amp; \to &amp; Y \\ \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\ X &amp; \to &amp; Z }
          %p such that for any other commutative square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ V &amp; \to &amp; Y \\ \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\ X &amp; \to &amp; Z }
          %p
            there is a cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to V
            and a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to P
            such that the induced composites
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to Y
            are equal.
          %p
            Now we can define a
            %strong unary congruence
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to consist of:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
            %li
              %p
                A parallel pair
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi t
                        %mo :
                        %mi R
                        %mo ⇉
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t:R\rightrightarrows X
            %li
              %p
                There exists a cover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:Y\to X
                and a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i:Y\to R
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mi t
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s i = t i = p
            %li
              %p
                There exists a cover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q:S\to R
                and a map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi v
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v:S\to R
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mi v
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s v = t q
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mi v
                        %mo =
                        %mi s
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t v = s q
            %li
              %p
                There exists a local unary pre-pullback
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                of the cospan
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi t
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi s
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \xrightarrow{t} X \xleftarrow{s} R
                and an arrow
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c:T\to R
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mi c
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s c = s \pi_1
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mi c
                        %mo =
                        %mi t
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t c = t \pi_2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2
                are the projections of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has a trivial topology, then local unary prelimits are simply weak limits, and this reduces to the definition of pseudo-equivalence relation. On the other hand, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is regular with its regular topology, then these conditions ensure exactly that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\to X\times X
            is an internal equivalence relation on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Now we can define morphisms between unary congruences using a suitable kind of either entire and functional relations or anafunctors, and obtain the exact completion of the unary site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman"} Shulman
          %h2#generalizations_to_higher_arity Generalizations to higher arity
          %p
            More generally, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-ary+site"} ∞-ary site
            has a
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-ary+exact+category"} ∞-ary exact category
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Shulman"} Shulman
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                When
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                        %mo =
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa=\omega
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos+completion"} pretopos completion
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+categories"} coherent categories
            %li
              %p
                When
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                is the size of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
                and constructs its
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+of+sheaves"} topos of sheaves
          %h2#properties_of_regular_and_exact_completions Properties of regular and exact completions
          %p
            Many categorical properties of interest are preserved by one or more of the regular and exact completions. That is, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has these properties, then so does the completion, and the inclusion functor preserves them. Note that frequently, for a completion to have some structure, it suffices for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to have a “weak” version of that structure.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Of course,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
                are preserved by all three completions. In fact, as we have remarked, for the ex/lex and reg/lex completions,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                need only have weak finite limits.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} lextensive
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is, and if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is, and in this case the embeddings preserve
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                (Menni 2000). It follows that if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_{ex/lex}
                is not a “pretopos functor” as it does not preserve
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epis"} regular epis
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is lextensive and has
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
                (and hence has finite colimits), then so do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                (Menni 2000). However, the inclusion functors do not preserve coequalizers. In fact, it suffices for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                to be lextensive with
                = succeed "," do
                  %em quasi-coequalizers
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g\colon Y\rightrightarrows X
                there exists
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\colon X\to Q
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi q
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q f = q g
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\colon X\to Z
                with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi h
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h f = h g
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
                coequalizes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pair"} kernel pair
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %li
              %p
                The categories
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                always have
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} enough (regular) projectives
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                are precisely the projective objects of these categories. Moreover, an exact category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                for some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                (with weak finite limits) if and only if it has enough projectives, in which case of course
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                can be taken to be the subcategory of projectives (Carboni–Vitale 1998). Note that if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                has enough projectives, then its subcategory of projectives always has weak finite limits. Similarly, a regular category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is of the form
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                for some
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                (with weak finite limits) if and only if it has enough projectives and every object can be embedded in a projective one.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a regular category satisfying the “regular”
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
                (i.e. every regular epi splits), then it is
                %em equivalent
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi reg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is exact and satisfies choice, then it is equivalent to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_{reg/lex}
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_{ex/lex}
                is an equivalence, then since the objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                are projective in these completions,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                must satisfy the axiom of choice.
              %p
                In fact, if we assume merely that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex} \to (C_{ex/lex})_{ex/lex}
                is a equivalence, then since the objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                are projective in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_{ex/lex})_{ex/lex}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to C_{ex/lex}
                is also an equivalence. It follows by induction that if the sequence of iterations of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_{ex/lex}
                stabilizes at any finite stage, it must in fact stabilize at the very beginning and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                must satisfy the axiom of choice. A similar argument applies to the reg/lex completion. (The ex/reg completion, of course, always stabilizes after one application.)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} Cartesian closure
                is preserved by the ex/lex completion (Carboni–Rosolini 2000). In fact,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is cartesian closed if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has
                = succeed "," do
                  %em weak simple products
                = succeed "s" do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    weak dependent product
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/weak+dependent+product"} ?
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                projections.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} Local cartesian closure
                is also preserved by the ex/lex completion (Carboni–Rosolini 2000). In fact,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is locally cartesian closed if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %em weakly locally cartesian closed
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
                has weak dependent products. It follows in particular that if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CE%A0-pretopos"} Π-pretopos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                = succeed "-pretopos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                we thus obtain a sequence
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi ex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi ex
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi ex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_{ex})_{ex}
                = succeed "-pretopoi," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            %li
              %p
                (Local) cartesian closure is seemingly not always preserved by the reg/lex completion, but it is under certain hypotheses. Recalling that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is the full subcategory of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                consisting of the kernel pairs, suppose that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has pullback-stable (epi,regular mono) factorizations and that every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+monomorphism"} regular
                congruence is a kernel pair. Then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                (BCRS 1998, Menni 2000): the reflection of a pseudo-equivalence relation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\rightrightarrows X
                is its (epi,regular mono) factorization. Moreover, the reflection preserves products, and also pullbacks along maps in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi reg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is cartesian closed or locally cartesian closed, so is
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi reg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
              %p
                Thus, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is weakly cartesian closed (resp. weakly locally cartesian closed), has pullback-stable (epi,regular mono) factorizations, and every regular congruence is a kernel pair, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is cartesian closed (resp. locally cartesian closed). In particular, the local versions of these hypotheses apply in particular to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                and to any
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{reg/lex}
                is called the category of
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equilogical+space"} equilogical space
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is lextensive with coequalizers (or “quasi-coequalizers”) and a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong-subobject+classifier"} strong-subobject classifier
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                (Menni 2000). It follows that if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a lextensive
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi reg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                we thus obtain a sequence
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi reg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi reg
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi reg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_{reg})_{reg}
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                = succeed "?" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi reg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
                = succeed "s?)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-type"} W-type
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CE%A0W-pretopos"} ΠW-pretopos
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                (see
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#vdB"} vandenBerg
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+topos"} elementary topos
                iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has weak dependent products and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generic+proof"} generic proof
                (
                %a{:href => "#Menni"}> Menni2000
                ). Note that if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a topos satisfying the axiom of choice, then its subobject classifier is a generic proof. It follows that in this case
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is a topos—but we already knew that, because
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is equivalent to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                for such a
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                Expanding on the last point, for a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi Set
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi D
                              %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = Set^{D^{op}}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is a topos iff
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                (
                %a{:href => "#Menni"}> Menni2000
                ).
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is regular, locally cartesian closed, and has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %em generic mono
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi ϒ
                      %mo →
                      %mi Λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau\colon \Upsilon\to \Lambda
                such that every monomorphism is a pullback of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi τ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
                (not necessarily uniquely), then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
                is a topos (
                %a{:href => "#Menni"}> Menni2000
                ).
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is an
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is an
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
          %p
            On the other hand, some properties are
            %em not
            preserved by the completions.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Of course, all the completions are regular categories, but the inclusions are not
                = succeed "s," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+functor"} regular functor
            %li
              %p
                We have seen that the existence of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
                or
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+objects"} power objects
                is not, in general, preserved by the completions (although if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a topos, then of course so is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi reg
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/reg}
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %li
              %p
                Similarly, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-powered
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                are. In particular, for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %mi reg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{C_{reg/lex}}(X)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %mi ex
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{C_{ex/lex}}(X)
                are equivalent to the preorder reflection of the slice category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
                = succeed "." do
                  %sup#fnref:1
                    %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is. However, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is additionally
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} lextensive
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/familial+regularity+and+exactness"} familial regularity and exactness
                for some clues on how to proceed.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is. However, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is additionally lextensive and locally cartesian closed, we have seen above that so are these completions, and hence Heyting (any lextensive locally cartesian closed regular category is Heyting).
            %li
              %p
                Unsurprisingly, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is, even if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is lextensive and LCC so that its completions are Heyting.
              %p
                In fact, a stronger statement is true: if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is lextensive and regular, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                are Boolean if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %em satisfies the axiom of choice
                (in which case they are of course equivalent to
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
                is such that every subobject of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                is complemented, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is projective in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi ex
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon Y\to X
                is a regular epi in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %mi reg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{C_{reg/lex}}(X)
                is the preorder reflection of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi reg
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi lex
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Z
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\colon Z\to X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %mi reg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{C_{reg/lex}}(X)
                are given by pullbacks in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
                admits a morphism to the initial object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is extensive. Now
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                is regular epi, hence so is its pullback
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to Z
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1+1
                implies that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\to 1
                is the equalizer of of the coprojections
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⇉
                        %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\rightrightarrows 1+1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                is an isomorphism; thus
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                is also initial. Now since joins in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sub
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %mi reg
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{C_{reg/lex}}(X)
                are given by coproducts in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo +
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y+Z \to X
                must become an isomorphism in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Sub
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mrow
                                %mi reg
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi lex
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub_{C_{reg/lex}}(X)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                is initial this means that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                itself has a section.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-pointed+topos"} well-pointed
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi reg
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{reg/lex}
                are (in the stronger sense appropriate for non-toposes). It is of course always true that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                is projective in the completions. And if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is lextensive, so that its completions are coherent, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                is indecomposable in them as soon as it is so in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                is a
                %em strong
                generator in the completions even if it is so in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                does.
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a well-pointed topos such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi lex
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{ex/lex}
                is also a topos, then the latter cannot be well-pointed unless
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                satisfies AC, because the completion would then be Boolean, and hence AC holds by the proof above.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p (to be written…)
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bishop+set"} Bishop sets
                is the ex/lex completion of the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hSet"} hSets
                in a theory without
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+sets"} quotients
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Realizability+toposes"} Realizability toposes
                arise as ex/lex completions of categories of partitioned assemblies based on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+combinatory+algebra"} partial combinatory algebra
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                (which turns out to be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
                of
                = succeed "-separated" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#Menni"} Menni
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TF
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TF
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion-free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
                is regular, but not exact. For instance, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} mod
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ (a,b) | a \equiv b \mod 2 \} \subseteq \mathbb{Z}\times\mathbb{Z}
                is not a kernel in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi TF
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TF
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TF
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TF
                is equivalent to the category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
                of all abelian groups.
              %p
                Note that although
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TF
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TF
                is not exact, its inclusion into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
                does have a left adjoint (quotient by torsion), and thus
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi TF
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} TF
                is cocomplete. Herein lies a subtle trap for the unwary: since the ex/reg completion monad is idempotent, it is in particular lax-idempotent, which means that any left adjoint to the unit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow C_{ex/reg}
                is in fact a (pseudo) algebra structure; but since the monad is actually idempotent, any algebra structure is an equivalence. Of course, the reflection
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo →
                      %mi TF
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab \to TF
                is
                %em not
                an equivalence, which doesn’t contract the general facts because this left adjoint is not a regular functor, and hence not an adjunction in the 2-category on which the monad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)_{ex/reg}
                lives. In fact, it is not hard to check that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ↪
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi ex
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow C_{ex/reg}
                has a left adjoint in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
                if and only if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
                (while if it has a left adjoint in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Reg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Reg
                then it must be an equivalence).
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
                of a (possibly large) finitely complete category, i.e., the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaves"} small presheaves
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cartesian+category"} free coproduct completion
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#JR"} here
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+exact+completion"} homotopy exact completion
          %h2#references References
          %ul#Menni
